{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310874,"nonce":"oQmNc6oVL9TJhXsoE/szyv8AFf8=","title":"website/build.mjs renders the Design Composer sources to static HTML — how it works, what is generated vs vendored, and the traps","message":"SHIPPED 6d3fb841. The redesign is authored in Design Composer `.dc.html`, which\nclient-renders from React + ReactDOM + Babel off unpkg — empty body to a\ncrawler, three blocking CDN requests, nowhere to put the indexed metadata.\n`website/build.mjs` (Node, zero deps) renders them to static HTML instead.\n\n**THE RULE THE OWNER SET: `website/_import/` IS VENDORED VERBATIM AND NEVER\nEDITED** — *\"you already have the htmls, don't reinvent anything\"*. Every\ntransformation lives in the builder. Changing a page means changing the\nbuilder or re-importing the design, never hand-editing the output.\n\nWHAT THE BUILDER DOES\n- Expands `sc-for` / `sc-if` / `{{ }}` into a compiled JS render function.\n  **The SAME function runs at build time and in the browser** — served HTML and\n  a re-render cannot drift.\n- Evaluates the design's `class Component extends DCLogic` in `node:vm` with a\n  stub base to get `renderVals()`. The component script is then carried into the\n  page unchanged, over a ~40-line shim (setState → morph). No Babel: the source\n  is already valid ES2020.\n- Interactivity re-renders the whole template and **morphs** into the live DOM\n  (attribute-level), so CSS width/colour transitions still run. Only `index` and\n  `architecture` ship a client.\n- `style-hover=` / `style-focus=` → generated classes. Every generated rule\n  needs `!important` — it is overriding an inline style attribute.\n- Mount point: `id=\"rz-root\"` is injected onto the design's FIRST element.\n  TRAP already hit: wrapping the root in an extra div made morph copy the\n  design root's attributes onto the wrapper and DELETE the id.\n\nBENCHMARK DATA (the owner's requirement: *\"benchmark data will be fed from the\nresults json\"*, *\"The Nue bench are static\"*)\n- `RUNS` + `WORKLOADS` are replaced from the newest `results_\u003cdate\u003e.json`;\n  `NUE_MODELS` / `NUE_PARITY` stay as authored.\n- The hardware caption is read from the same file's `system_info`, so numbers\n  and machine can never describe different runs. The design's caption sentence\n  is a hard anchor — **the build THROWS if the design rewords it** rather than\n  leave a stale machine on the page.\n- `website.yml` runs `build.mjs --results artifacts/benchmark-results`, and\n  `_import/`, `.seo/`, `build.mjs` are rsync-excluded from `_site`.\n- Target-name map lives in `CHART_TARGETS`; CI emits `haxe-hashlink`,\n  `haxe-hashlink-c`, `haxe-cpp`, `haxe-jvm`, `rayzor-{tiered,llvm,cranelift,\n  gcc,precompiled,precompiled-tiered}`.\n\nRESPONSIVE (added after *\"Still terrible in mobile\"*)\nThe design is desktop-width inline styles. The builder reads each element's\nstatic style and emits narrow-viewport classes: grids drop columns, font-size\n≥30px becomes `clamp`, gutters narrow, `border-right` on a collapsed grid's\nchild becomes `border-bottom`. Breakpoints 1024/900/860/760/680.\n- Header nav is behind a **checkbox+label toggle** (`.rz-burger`), not JS — the\n  doc pages ship no client at all. External links and the search input carry\n  `.rz-menu-item` and move into the opened panel so the bar stays one row.\n- TRAP: a blanket `flex-wrap:wrap` on every gapped flex row made label/value\n  rows wrap inconsistently by text length. Gate is now `gap ≥ 20px` OR the row\n  sets `justify-content`.\n\nVERIFY WITH HEADLESS CHROME, NOT BY READING CSS. `/Applications/Google\nChrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome --headless --dump-dom` plus a probe\npage that loads each page in a sized iframe.\n- **`--window-size` does NOT set the layout viewport for `--screenshot`** — a\n  390px capture of an 800px layout looks broken and is a lie. Put the page in\n  an iframe of the target width inside a wide window.\n- Measure overflow with `html/body { overflow-x: visible !important }` forced\n  on, or the base stylesheet's own clipping hides it.\n- Bars animate via IntersectionObserver; `scrollIntoView` inside a nested\n  iframe does NOT trigger it. Load `index.html#benchmarks` instead.\n\nSEO: five pages, per-page title/description/canonical, site-level og/icons/\ntheme-color, JSON-LD on home only. `.seo/README.md` records what carried over\nand what was deliberately changed. Title/tagline are now\n**\"Rayzor — Faster Haxe, Native Performance\"** — the owner rejected LLVM and\nbackend names in the tagline: *\"I need something searchable in Google\"*.\nBackend vocabulary lives in `keywords` and JSON-LD `featureList`. Neither is a\nranking signal; title, description and headings are.\n\nSee [[project_compiler_frontend_codegen_split]] and\n[[project_ast_lowering_modularization_chore]] — both were queued behind this.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_website_static_build_from_design` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}